      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Kansas City was first founded at the spot that later became River Market, making the area the city’s original landing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://kcrivermarket.com/history-of-the-kansas-city-river-market/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Centropolis Hotel, built in 1880 at 5th and Grand, was named after William Gilpin’s proposed title for Kansas City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Market%2C_Kansas_City",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Pacific House Hotel, erected in 1860, later hosted legends like Jesse James and Wyatt Earp during River Market’s early days.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Market%2C_Kansas_City",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Kansas City’s first streetcar line began in 1870 at Fourth and Main in City Market, running to Westport before becoming a cable rail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
